summary:
  Re-fetch all asks the row's own logo in its kind's place, not first.

history:
  The row's own logo goes first so it is weighed against every find and kept
  on a tie; asked later, the hunt can stop before it is asked at all.

target:
  package/contents/ui/FaviconLogic.js

find:
          if (c.kind === "current") { lanes[0].push(u); continue; }

replace:
          if (c.kind === "current") { lanes[4].push(u); continue; }

expect:
  Killed by tst_faviconlogic::test_a_hunt_keeps_the_logo_a_row_has_unless_something_beats_it.
  Line-neutral.
